.SH NAME
primes \- generate primes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B primes
[\fIstart\fP Op \fIstop\fP]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B primes
utility prints primes in ascending order, one per line, starting
at or above
\fIstart\fP
and continuing until, but not including
\fIstop .\fP
The
\fIstart\fP
value must be at least 0 and not greater than
\fIstop .\fP
The
\fIstop\fP
value must not be greater than 4294967295.
The default value of
\fIstop\fP
is 4294967295.
.PP
When the
.B primes
utility is invoked with no arguments,
\fIstart\fP
is read from standard input.
\fIstop\fP
is taken to be 4294967295.
The
\fIstart\fP
value may be preceded by a single
'\&+ .'
The
\fIstart\fP
value is terminated by a non-digit character (such as a newline).
The input line must not be longer than 255 characters.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Out of range or invalid input results in
an appropriate error message
being written to standard error.
.SH BUGS
.B primes
won't get you a world record.

